# Design Tokens

## Color Palette
Never hardcode hex values. Use Tailwind token classes or CSS variables:

| Token | Value | Tailwind Class |
|---|---|---|
| Primary Green | `#2d5a3d` | `text-primary`, `bg-primary`, `border-primary` |
| Accent Gold | `#c4a35a` | `text-accent`, `bg-accent`, `border-accent` |
| Cream | `#f7f3eb` | `text-cream`, `bg-cream` |
| Dark | `#1a1a16` | `text-dark`, `bg-dark` |
| Muted | `#6b6b5e` | `text-muted`, `bg-muted` |

CSS variables available globally:
```css
var(--color-primary)  /* #2d5a3d */
var(--color-accent)   /* #c4a35a */
var(--color-cream)    /* #f7f3eb */
var(--color-dark)     /* #1a1a16 */
var(--color-muted)    /* #6b6b5e */
```

## Typography
Use Tailwind typography classes only — never hardcode `font-family`, `font-size`, or `font-weight`:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<h1 style={{ fontSize: '48px', fontWeight: 700, fontFamily: 'Playfair Display' }}>

// ✅ GOOD
<h1 className="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-dark">
```

- `font-display` — Fraunces (headings / brand)
- `font-sans` — DM Sans (body / UI)

## Spacing & Shadows
Use the extended Tailwind / theme scale — never raw px/rem values in className strings for colors or fonts.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded color
<button className="bg-[#2d5a3d] text-[#f7f3eb]">

// ✅ GOOD — design token
<button className="bg-primary text-cream">
```
